<title>LATVIA: SEVERAL BIG BANK SECURITY LICENCES EXTENDED.</title>
<headline>SEVERAL BIG BANK SECURITY LICENCES EXTENDED.</headline>
<dateline>RIGA 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The securities commission said on Monday that it has extended the securities' dealing licences of Savings Bank, Zemes Banka, the Latvian Investment Bank and Pareks Bank by one year.</p>
<p>The licence of broker Inveks was also extended, the commission said in a statement.</p>
<p>However, the commission postponed a decision on re-registering the licence of Fincross Securities until the company had handed in the correct documents.</p>
<p>-- Riga newsroom, +371 721 5240</p>
</text>
